<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. van Gogh returns two weeks after his first visit, four weeks after aripiprazole 10 mg was started in hospital, and is seen by Dr. Feld of the coordinated specialty care team on the same day. He has taken every dose. He has had no confusion and hears nothing by day, but on some nights he still hears his name called as he falls asleep, and on those nights he feels for a while that people in the street are talking about him; by morning he knows this is not so. He sleeps about six hours with breaks. His mood is a little better: he feels less ashamed and has started to sketch, but still cannot paint for long. The passive thoughts that it would be easier not to wake up come less often; he has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. He drinks two or three glasses of wine most evenings and no spirits since discharge. He has noticed no restlessness or stiffness. He had his brain MRI and EEG this morning, after a night of shortened sleep as instructed. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Aripiprazole</td><td>10 mg daily for four weeks, every dose taken</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotic symptoms</td><td>Hears his name called at sleep onset on some nights, with brief suspiciousness; none by day</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Somewhat better; PHQ-9 11; item 9 scored 1, less often</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About six hours, broken</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Two or three glasses of wine most evenings; no spirits</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>None noticed</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

